¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Many pastors have destroyed my vineyard, they have trodden my portion under foot, they have made my pleasant portion a desolate wilderness.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡They have made it desolate, and being desolate it mourneth unto me; the whole land is made desolate, because no man layeth it to heart.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄThe spoilers are come upon all high places through the wilderness: for the sword of the LORD shall devour from the one end of the land even to the other end of the land: no flesh shall have peace.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸They have sown wheat, but shall reap thorns: they have put themselves to pain, but shall not profit: and they shall be ashamed of your revenues because of the fierce anger of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàThus saith the LORD against all mine evil neighbours, that touch the inheritance which I have caused my people Israel to inherit; Behold, I will pluck them out of their land, and pluck out the house of Judah from among them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºAnd it shall come to pass, after that I have plucked them out I will return, and have compassion on them, and will bring them again, every man to his heritage, and every man to his land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÔAnd it shall come to pass, if they will diligently learn the ways of my people, to swear by my name, The LORD liveth; as they taught my people to swear by Baal; then shall they be built in the midst of my people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[But if they will not obey, I will utterly pluck up and destroy that nation, saith the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse